## Day 8 — Broken Access Control + IDOR + Burp Suite

### Broken Access Control — OWASP A01:2025
- #1 most common vulnerability — found in 94% of apps
- Authentication = who you are
- Authorization = what you're allowed to do
- BAC = authentication works but authorization fails

### IDOR Types
- Horizontal: access other users' data at same privilege level
- Vertical: access higher privilege data (admin)
- Blind: action succeeds on someone else's object with no visible response

### IDOR Testing Method
1. Find any parameter with an ID (user_id, order_id, file_id)
2. Intercept in Burp Suite
3. Change the ID to another value
4. If different user's data returns = IDOR confirmed

### Burp Suite Tools Learned
- Proxy: intercept and modify live requests
- Repeater: resend modified requests without browser
- Intruder: automate brute force attacks
- Decoder: encode/decode URL, Base64, HTML

### Fix for IDOR
- Server-side ownership check on every request
- Verify logged-in user owns the requested resource
- Never trust client-supplied IDs without verification
